  "note": "dailyQueryCapAllPriorities' committed witness, and the defect it closes. Three commitments in one working day — a proposal in the morning, an audit after lunch, release notes in the afternoon — with a break, a presentation, an idle span and one real accusation. The per-priority cap alone would license twelve questions across three priorities and would be bounded only by the shared budget at seven; the day cap stops the fifth question being followed by a sixth, and it stops it under a FRESH priority whose own cap has barely been touched, which is exactly the shape of the hole. The number a person feels is questions-per-day, so that is the number with a constant, a fixture and a gated metric.",
